  "question": {
    "text": "When two progressive waves $y_1=4 \\sin (2 x-6 t) \\quad$ and $y_2=3 \\sin \\left(2 x-6 t-\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) \\quad$ are superimposed, the amplitude of the resultant wave is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "Phase difference between the two waves is $90^{\\circ}$. Amplitudes are added by vector method.\n$\\therefore$ Answer is 5 .",
